{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example",title:"Worked example 3",say:`Bypassed, the analyzer sees only ${P('NO')}: three hundred eighty. In line, four hundred twenty, so forty look like nitrogen dioxide. The converter works at ninety-two percent: forty over point nine two, forty-three point five.`,cues:{fk:'Bypassed, the analyzer',k1:'In line, four',k1b:'so forty look',k2:'The converter works',k2b:'forty over point'},q:['CLD: 380 ppm with the NO₂ converter bypassed, 420 ppm with it in line; η = 0.92.','Find the true NO₂, the true NOx and how much the bench under-reports.'],f:['apparent NO₂ = NOx (apparent) − NO','true NO₂ = apparent NO₂ ÷ η'],hint:'Bypassed, the CLD sees NO only.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Apparent NO₂", ["420 − 380","apparent NO₂ = 40 ppm"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["True NO₂", ["40 ÷ 0.92 = 43.48","true NO₂ = 43.5 ppm"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["True NOx", ["380 + 43.5","true NOx = 423.5 ppm"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Under-report", ["423.5 − 420","3.5 ppm low, about 0.8 %"], ["k4","k4b"]]],live:[0,1]},
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example (NOx)",title:"Worked example 3",say:`Add it to the ${P('NO')}: true NOx is four hundred twenty-three point five. The uncorrected bench reads three point five parts per million low, about point eight percent.`,pause:1,cues:{fk:'Add it to',k3:'Add it to',k3b:'true NOx is',k4:'The uncorrected bench',k4b:'about point eight',a:'about point eight'},q:['CLD: 380 ppm with the NO₂ converter bypassed, 420 ppm with it in line; η = 0.92.','Find the true NO₂, the true NOx and how much the bench under-reports.'],f:['apparent NO₂ = NOx (apparent) − NO','true NO₂ = apparent NO₂ ÷ η'],hint:'Bypassed, the CLD sees NO only.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Apparent NO₂", ["420 − 380","apparent NO₂ = 40 ppm"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["True NO₂", ["40 ÷ 0.92 = 43.48","true NO₂ = 43.5 ppm"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["True NOx", ["380 + 43.5","true NOx = 423.5 ppm"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Under-report", ["423.5 − 420","3.5 ppm low, about 0.8 %"], ["k4","k4b"]]],live:[2,3],ans:['True NO₂ 43.5 ppm; true NOx 423.5 ppm; the bench reads 3.5 ppm low','a']},
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example 4",title:"Worked example 4",say:`Now an infrared ${P('CO')} analyzer. Beer-Lambert makes the log of the transmission proportional to concentration. The span gas gives minus point three five six seven. The sample gives minus point two two three one.`,cues:{fk:'Beer-Lambert makes',k1:'The span gas',k1b:'minus point three',k2:'The sample gives',k2b:'minus point two'},q:['NDIR CO: I/I₀ = 0.70 with a 2.0 % CO span gas, 0.80 with the engine sample.','Find the CO in the sample, assuming Beer–Lambert behaviour.'],f:['I/I₀ = e<tspan baseline-shift="super" font-size="70%">−acL</tspan>, so ln(I/I₀) ∝ c'],hint:'Same cell, same gas: a and L cancel in the ratio.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Span gas, 2.0 % CO", ["ln 0.70","ln 0.70 = −0.3567"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["Engine sample", ["ln 0.80","ln 0.80 = −0.2231"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["CO in the sample", ["2.0 % × (−0.2231) ÷ (−0.3567) = 2.0 × 0.6255","c = 1.25 % CO"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Straight-line guess", ["2.0 × (1 − 0.80) ÷ (1 − 0.70)","1.33 %: too high, the response is not linear"], ["k4","k4b"]]],live:[0,1]},
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example 4 (CO)",title:"Worked example 4",say:'Scale the span by the ratio of logs: two percent times point six two five five, one point two five percent. A straight-line guess, one point three three, is too high: the response is not linear.',pause:1,cues:{fk:'Scale the span',k3:'Scale the span',k3b:'one point two five percent',k4:'A straight-line guess',k4b:'one point three three',a:'the response is'},q:['NDIR CO: I/I₀ = 0.70 with a 2.0 % CO span gas, 0.80 with the engine sample.','Find the CO in the sample, assuming Beer–Lambert behaviour.'],f:['I/I₀ = e<tspan baseline-shift="super" font-size="70%">−acL</tspan>, so ln(I/I₀) ∝ c'],hint:'Same cell, same gas: a and L cancel in the ratio.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Span gas, 2.0 % CO", ["ln 0.70","ln 0.70 = −0.3567"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["Engine sample", ["ln 0.80","ln 0.80 = −0.2231"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["CO in the sample", ["2.0 % × (−0.2231) ÷ (−0.3567) = 2.0 × 0.6255","c = 1.25 % CO"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Straight-line guess", ["2.0 × (1 − 0.80) ÷ (1 − 0.70)","1.33 %: too high, the response is not linear"], ["k4","k4b"]]],live:[2,3],ans:['The sample holds 1.25 % CO','a']},
{s:2,k:'trap2',term:'Exam trap',title:'Exam trap!',say:`Exam trap. The ${P('FID')} counts carbon atoms. Don't read ninety parts per million carbon as ninety of propane. Write the division by three carbons: thirty parts per million.`,cues:{x:'Exam trap',w:"Don't read ninety",r:'Write the division'},wl:"Don't write",rl:'Write',wrong:['FID reads 90 ppmC of propane,','so propane = 90 ppm'],right:['Propane C₃H₈ has 3 carbons:','90 ppmC ÷ 3 = 30 ppm propane'],wv:(c,u,b)=>`
${EM_T(320,44,'one reading per molecule?',{fs:26,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:TRED})}
${[170,250,330].map(x=>`<circle cx="${x}" cy="130" r="30" fill="#495057"/>`+EM_T(x,140,'C',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:'#FFFFFF'})).join('')}${EM_L(200,130,220,130,'#495057',6)}${EM_L(280,130,300,130,'#495057',6)}
${EM_T(250,210,'propane',{fs:24,fw:700,a:'middle',fill:EM_GREY})}
${EM_T(420,140,'= 1 count?',{fs:28,fw:800,fill:TRED})}
${EM_T(320,290,'90 ppmC → 90 ppm propane',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:TRED})}`,rv:(c,u,b)=>`
${[170,250,330].map(x=>`<circle cx="${x}" cy="100" r="30" fill="#495057"/>`+EM_T(x,110,'C',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:'#FFFFFF'})+EM_T(x,168,'+',{fs:34,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})).join('')}${EM_L(200,100,220,100,'#495057',6)}${EM_L(280,100,300,100,'#495057',6)}
${EM_T(420,96,'3 carbons',{fs:26,fw:800,fill:GRN})}${EM_T(420,130,'= 3 ion counts',{fs:24,fw:700,fill:EM_GREY})}
${EM_T(320,232,'ppmC = ppm × carbon number',{fs:24,fw:700,a:'middle',fill:EM_GREY})}
${EM_T(320,290,'90 ÷ 3 = 30 ppm propane',{fs:30,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})}`},
/* ---- recap ---- */
{s:RC,k:'recap',term:'Recap',say:'Recap in three. Stop pollutants forming: EGR and retard cool the flame. Treat the exhaust: a three-way catalyst at lambda one, or the diesel line in order. And measure each gas by its own effect, then correct it.',cues:{r1:'Stop pollutants forming',r2:'Treat the exhaust',r3:'And measure each'},panels:[["Stop it forming","BLU",'emR1',['EGR and retard cool the flame:','NOx falls, PM can rise.'],'r1'],["Treat the exhaust","ORG",'emR2',['Petrol: one TWC at λ = 1.','Diesel: DOC, DPF, urea, SCR, ASC.'],'r2'],["Measure each gas","GRN",'emR3',['NDIR, O₂ cell, CLD, FID, smoke.','Correct: ÷ η, ÷ carbon number.'],'r3']],live:[0,1,2]},
/* ---- exam practice ---- */
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why does EGR lower NOx but raise PM?",say:'Question one. Why does EGR lower NOx, but raise particulate matter?',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'Why does EGR'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why does EGR lower NOx but raise PM?",say:`EGR swaps oxygen for carbon dioxide and water, which absorb heat. A cooler flame with less oxygen makes less ${P('NO')}. The same conditions slow soot burn-out, so particulate matter rises.`,cues:{a1:'EGR swaps oxygen',a2:'The same conditions'},al:[["EGR swaps O₂ for CO₂ and H₂O, which absorb heat: a cooler flame with less O₂, so less NO forms.",'a1'],["The same low temperature and O₂ slow soot burn-out, so PM rises.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>`
${EM_T(155,40,'without EGR',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:EM_GREY})}${EM_T(465,40,'with EGR',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU})}
${EM_cyl(70,64,170,330,286,40)}${EM_cyl(380,64,170,330,286,40)}
${EM_flame(155,170,130,ORG)}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),EM_flame(465,190,96,'#FFA94D')+EM_mol(420,100,'CO₂',BLU,20)+EM_mol(512,100,'H₂O',BLU,20)+EM_mol(108,262,'NO',TRED,20)+EM_mol(202,262,'NO',TRED,20)+EM_mol(465,262,'NO',TRED,20)+EM_T(155,384,'hot: NO high',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:TRED})+EM_T(465,384,'cooler: NO low',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),EM_soot([[410,150],[520,160],[402,214],[530,222],[412,262],[518,262]])+EM_T(465,440,'soot left: PM rises',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:EM_SOOT})+EM_T(155,440,'soot burnt out',{fs:24,fw:700,a:'middle',fill:EM_GREY}))}`},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"CO2 is 0.04 % ambient, 1.50 % in the intake and 10.0 % in the exhaust. Find the EGR share of the charge.",say:'Question two. Carbon dioxide is point zero four percent ambient, one point five in the intake, and ten in the exhaust. Find the EGR share of the charge.',cues:{k:'Question two',q:'Carbon dioxide is'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"CO2 is 0.04 % ambient, 1.50 % in the intake and 10.0 % in the exhaust. Find the EGR share of the charge.",say:'Intake rise: one point five minus point zero four, one point four six. Full rise: ten minus point zero four, nine point nine six. Divide them: fourteen point seven percent.',cues:{fk:'Intake rise',k1:'one point five minus',k1b:'one point four six',k2:'Full rise',k2b:'nine point nine six',k3:'Divide them',k3b:'fourteen point seven'},calc:{f:['x = intake rise ÷ full rise','rise = CO₂ − CO₂ ambient'],hint:'Subtract the ambient CO₂ from both, not the intake.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Intake rise",["1.50 − 0.04","intake rise = 1.46 %"],["k1","k1b"]],["Full rise",["10.0 − 0.04","full rise = 9.96 %"],["k2","k2b"]],["EGR share",["1.46 ÷ 9.96 = 0.147","EGR = 14.7 % of the charge"],["k3","k3b"]]],live:[0,1,2]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"A three-way catalyst is fitted to a lean-burn petrol engine running at λ = 1.4. Which gases are converted and which are not? Suggest a fix.",say:'Question three. A three-way catalyst goes on a lean-burn petrol engine at lambda one point four. Which gases are converted, which are not, and what is the fix?',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'A three-way catalyst'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"A three-way catalyst is fitted to a lean-burn petrol engine running at λ = 1.4. Which gases are converted and which are not? Suggest a fix.",say:`${P('CO')} and hydrocarbons are oxidized: oxygen is plentiful. NOx is not reduced, because the spare oxygen uses up the ${P('CO')}, hydrogen and hydrocarbons that would reduce it. The fix: a lean NOx trap with rich purges, or urea SCR.`,cues:{a1:'and hydrocarbons are',a2:'NOx is not',a3:'The fix'},al:[["CO and HC are oxidised, since oxygen is plentiful.",'a1'],["NOx is not reduced: the spare O₂ uses up the CO, H₂ and HC that would reduce it.",'a2'],["Fix: a lean NOx trap with short rich purges, or urea SCR.",'a3']],vis:(c,u,b)=>`
${EM_T(310,40,'λ = 1.4: spare oxygen',{fs:26,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU})}
${EM_brick(220,90,180,190,EM_STEEL)}${EM_T(310,310,'TWC',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:EM_STEEL})}
${EM_mol(84,110,'CO, HC',ORG,22)}${EM_mol(84,190,'O₂',BLU,22)}${EM_mol(84,260,'NOx',TRED,22)}
${EM_arrow(150,110,214,110,EM_GREY,3)}${EM_arrow(150,190,214,190,EM_GREY,3)}${EM_arrow(150,260,214,260,EM_GREY,3)}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),EM_arrow(406,120,456,120,GRN,4)+EM_mol(530,120,'CO₂, H₂O',GRN,20)+EM_ok(530,166,GRN))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),EM_arrow(406,250,456,250,TRED,4)+EM_mol(530,250,'NOx',TRED,22)+EM_no(530,300,TRED)+EM_T(530,344,'passes',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:TRED}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a3'),EM_box(40,380,540,90,{fill:'#EBFBEE',st:GRN,sw:3})+EM_T(310,418,'add a lean NOx trap',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})+EM_T(310,452,'(rich purges) or urea SCR',{fs:22,fw:700,a:'middle',fill:EM_GREY}))}`},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:'Your free notes are the PDF linked in the description. Redraw the EGR loop, the diesel line and the bench, then check the numbers.',cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the EGR'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["The two chapters", "Emission control: in-cylinder and after-treatment methods; Emission measurement: NDIR, chemiluminescence, FID and smoke meters"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["The EGR loop and the diesel line", "Cooled exhaust fed back lifts the intake CO₂ from 0.04 to 1.80 %: 14.7 % EGR. Then DOC, DPF, urea, SCR and slip catalyst, in that order."], ["The emission bench", "Smoke meter on raw gas, heated FID on hot wet gas, NDIR, O₂ cell and CLD on dried gas; the CLD reads 380 and 420 ppm, η = 0.92."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: John B. Heywood (Internal Combustion Engine Fundamentals); Willard W. Pulkrabek (Engineering Fundamentals of the Internal Combustion Engine)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:'So remember: cool the flame or clean the exhaust, match the catalyst to the mixture, and correct every reading. Next time, emission standards and driving cycles. See you there!',cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'cool the flame',w2:'match the catalyst',w3:'and correct every',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['COOL IT OR CLEAN IT','BLU','w1'],['CATALYST FITS THE MIXTURE','ORG','w2'],['CORRECT EVERY READING','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next lesson", "Emission standards and driving cycles", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
